# TODO — unported sections of 0001-nuxel-phone-features.patch for
#        linux-postmarketos-qcom-msm8953
#
# This file records the sections of the Nuxel phone-features patch that are
# NOT yet ported to the msm8953 tree, and WHY they cannot apply as-is.
# Once each section is ported, delete this .TODO file and replace
# patches/0001-nuxel-phone-features.patch with the real ported patch.
#
# Missing upstream symbol/context (the blocker):
#   The msm8953-mainline tree has NO drivers/nuxel/ directory and NO
#   CONFIG_NUXEL / CONFIG_NUXEL_PHONE / CONFIG_NUXEL_BOOT_PARAM Kconfig
#   symbols. The original patch (6.12 GKI tree) adds all three from scratch,
#   and its drivers/Kconfig + drivers/Makefile wiring hunks rely on context
#   lines whose surrounding content differs between the 6.12 GKI tree and the
#   5.x-era msm8953 tree. `git apply --check` against the cloned tree decides
#   whether the context still matches; the hunks below are expected to need a
#   manual re-base.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Section 1 — drivers/Kconfig wiring hunk (unported)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream diff (approx.):
#   --- a/drivers/Kconfig
#   +++ b/drivers/Kconfig
#   @@ ... @@
#    source "drivers/opp/Kconfig"
#   +source "drivers/nuxel/Kconfig"
#    source "drivers/siox/Kconfig"
#
# Why it fails / what is missing:
#   Context-dependent. The msm8953 branch has its own drivers/Kconfig history;
#   the opp/siox context lines may not be adjacent. Re-base by hand if needed.
#   The symbol that must exist afterwards: CONFIG_NUXEL (new, drivers/nuxel/Kconfig).

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Section 2 — drivers/Makefile wiring hunk (unported)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Upstream diff (approx.):
#   --- a/drivers/Makefile
#   +++ b/drivers/Makefile
#   @@ ... @@
#    obj-$(CONFIG_DPLL)               += dpll/
#   +obj-$(CONFIG_NUXEL)              += nuxel/
#
# Why it fails / what is missing:
#   Context-dependent (same as Section 1). The msm8953 Makefile may order
#   entries differently. The symbol that must exist afterwards: obj-$(CONFIG_NUXEL)
#   pointing at drivers/nuxel/.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Section 3 — drivers/nuxel/Kconfig (unported; new file)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Adds the three Nuxel symbols. Required content for the port:
#   config NUXEL
#       tristate "Nuxel device support"
#       default y
#       help
#         Nuxel phone framework. Parses nuxel.device= (mustang / s10plus /
#         g7power) and nuxel.boot=1 on the kernel command line.
#   config NUXEL_PHONE
#       bool "Nuxel phone feature set"
#       depends on NUXEL
#   config NUXEL_BOOT_PARAM
#       bool "Nuxel boot-parameter parsing"
#       depends on NUXEL
#
# Missing upstream symbol: none of CONFIG_NUXEL / CONFIG_NUXEL_PHONE /
# CONFIG_NUXEL_BOOT_PARAM exist in the msm8953 tree.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Section 4 — drivers/nuxel/Makefile (unported; new file)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#   obj-$(CONFIG_NUXEL) += nuxel-core.o

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Section 5 — drivers/nuxel/nuxel-core.c (unported; new file)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The C driver uses struct proc_ops (mainline since v5.6) and
# saved_command_line (exported by init/do_mounts.c) — both expected to exist
# in the 5.x-era msm8953 tree, so this section is expected to port with only
# the help/description strings changed (mustang -> g7power). Verify after the
# wiring hunks apply.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# How to check current status (after `bash kernel/g7power/build-kernel.sh --clone`):
#   git -C kernel/g7power/.build/src apply --check \
#       kernel/g7power/patches/0001-nuxel-phone-features.patch
# If it applies cleanly: port done — delete this file and uncomment the
# CONFIG_NUXEL* lines in kernel/g7power/defconfig.
